<title>AUSTRALIA: Sedimentary says to trial uranium mines.</title>
<headline>Sedimentary says to trial uranium mines.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sedimentary Holdings NL said production trials at new uranium deposits in South Australia are scheduled to start within 12 months following settlement of an agreement with MIM Holdings Ltd to buy the properties.</p>
<p>Sedimentary said it now holds a 35 percent equity interest in Southern Cross Resources Inc of Canada, which through its wholly-owned Southern Cross Resources Australia Pty ltd, will develop the Honeymoon, Goulds Dam and Yarramba uranium projects.</p>
<p>&quot;Production trials using proven in-situ leaching techniques are expected to commence within 12 months,&quot; Sedimentary said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
